<title>GERMANY: BASF to invest 100 mln dmk in bio-tech JV.</title>
<headline>BASF to invest 100 mln dmk in bio-tech JV.</headline>
<dateline>LUDWIGSHAFEN, Germany 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>German chemicals group BASF AG on Wednesday said it will invest 100 million marks in a new biotechnology joint venture it has entered into with U.S. group Lynx Therapeutics.</p>
<p>BASF will hold a 51 percent stake in the joint venture with the Hayward, California, based Lynx group holding a 49 percent stake, BASF said.</p>
<p>The joint venture will operate in Germany and initially employ 60 people.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
